\title{showkitr: Before/After Showcase Cards for Function Calls}
\description{
Two tools for teaching and sharing R functions. fx_showcase() runs a function call, captures its before/after state, and composites a styled before/after image for sharing (e.g. "function of the day" posts); an RStudio Addin wraps a selected call with it in place. fx_glossary() and fx_glossary_page() turn a function's help page into student-friendly glossary cards (arguments, defaults, plain-language descriptions) as standalone HTML, with optional hand-written wording from a YAML file.
